{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sorry, one second, this thing froze again. What brings you in today?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): I'm Linda, his wife. Carl's seventy-eight. For a few months now he asks me the same questions over and over.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He has, though. He also forgot two appointments last month, the dentist and then the eye doctor.",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0006] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sorry, say that part again? Screen jumped. The appointments?",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Two appointments, last month. He forgot both.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): And about three weeks ago he got lost driving to the market on Oak Street. I picked him up at the hardware store lot. They had a sale, place was packed, not that that matters.",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (PATIENT): Didn't.",
  "[SEG0010] person_1 (DOCTOR): Carl, that didn't happen?",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0012] person_1 (DOCTOR): Okay. Um. Headaches at all?",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0014] person_1 (DOCTOR): Chest pain? Shortness of breath?",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0016] person_1 (DOCTOR): Linda, has he fallen?",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Mm, I suppose. Sometimes, not really.",
  "[SEG0018] person_1 (DOCTOR): I was clicking through the chart. Say that once more?",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Not really. I don't think so.",
  "[SEG0020] person_1 (DOCTOR): Who handles his pills?",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): I do. I set them out every morning, otherwise the bottles get mixed up.",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (PATIENT): Her.",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (DOCTOR): What are the medicines?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Lisinopril ten, well actually twenty milligrams every morning for his blood pressure. Metformin five hundred milligrams twice a day for the diabetes. And atorvastatin forty at night.",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (DOCTOR): Atorvastatin, the dose again? It didn't save.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Forty milligrams, at bedtime.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (DOCTOR): The blood pressure and the diabetes, those are ongoing?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Yes. Both of them, for years.",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0030] person_1 (DOCTOR): Just the two of you at home?",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Yes, just us.",
  "[SEG0032] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any allergies to medicines?",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): No. None.",
  "[SEG0034] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0035] person_1 (DOCTOR): Pressure at check-in... I'm seeing one fifty-two over ninety. No, that's an old reading. Today is one thirty-six over seventy-eight.",
  "[SEG0036] person_1 (DOCTOR): People jump to dementia, or a thyroid issue, or low B12, or the medicines doing it. I am not concluding any of that. No diagnosis from me today. Let's see what the tests say.",
  "[SEG0037] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'll order bloodwork, with the thyroid and a B12 in it, and I'll set up a memory assessment.",
  "[SEG0038] person_1 (DOCTOR): Hold off on driving until we've checked this. Come back in three weeks.",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Alright. I'll keep the keys. Thanks."
 ],
